WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.800
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the Frozen 2 deleted

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.490
scenes that completely changed the end of
the movie,

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:12.410
including a heart-breaking message from Anna
and Elsa's parents, and an awesome song for

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.360
Kristoff that we never got to see.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:19.690
Frozen 2 took some dark turns; however, the
movie's original ending was going to be even

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:25.140
darker with the destruction of Arendelle Castle
and even the possible death of Elsa.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:30.220
At the end of Frozen 2, Anna makes a momentous
decision on how to restore peace to the land:

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.880
"We have to break the dam."

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.129
"But Arendelle will be flooded."

00:00:33.129 --> 00:00:37.670
She provokes the Earth Giants into destroying
the dam which causes a huge tidal wave that's

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:42.820
about to engulf Arendelle until a reanimated
Elsa arrives and creates a giant ice barrier

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.820
to stop it.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.670
However, a deleted scene on the Blu-ray now
shows that in an earlier version of the movie,

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:53.239
Elsa wasn't there to stop the tsunami which
went on destroy Arendelle Castle and probably

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:55.100
flooded much of the kingdom.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:59.999
The deleted scene takes place as Anna, Elsa
and Kristoff assess what to do in the aftermath

00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:02.120
of the devastation caused by the flood.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.840
"We'll rebuild the castle.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.719
New, no secrets, no deceit, new rules even!"

00:01:07.719 --> 00:01:11.750
This original ending would have been a little
darker as the consequences of the Arendelle's

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:16.000
betrayal of the Northuldra would have had
a much greater impact on the kingdom.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.950
The Art of Frozen 2 book also gives more details
on what happened afterwards in this original

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:25.780
ending, explaining that the castle would have
been rebuilt in "a combination of the Northuldra

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.460
and Arendellian styles."

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:32.500
In this alternate ending, Anna also says she'll
do away with the old lies and secrets and

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.689
create brand new rules.

00:01:34.689 --> 00:01:39.150
That last point is likely a reference back
to another deleted scene in which Anna and

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:43.820
Elsa discover a hidden room in the castle,
and inside they uncover secret books and journals

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.100
belonging to their mother.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:49.130
"These next pages are in English, but also..

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.130
Northuldrian."

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.130
"Northuldrian?

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.090
But that language is forbidden.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.340
Why would mother know it?

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.890
Or dare use it?"

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:01.060
It sounds like the repression of Northuldra
culture in Arendelle was even more extensive

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.870
than we saw in the film, and now as she's
aware of both this and her own mixed heritage,

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:10.690
it's clear that in this alternate ending Queen
Anna planned to abolish this type of discrimination.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:14.980
"Our lands and people, now connected by love."

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:19.569
There's another part to this original ending
in which Elsa uses her magic for Anna to bring

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:24.370
back a memory of her parents, revealing just
how highly they thought of their younger daughter.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:25.640
"I wanna show you something."

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.790
"Wow."

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:32.650
"Darling, I've been thinking."

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:33.650
"Oh!"

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.459
"It might be time to tell Anna about Elsa.

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:39.090
I can't bear keeping her shut out any more.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.599
She's maturing now, she can be responsible."

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:43.720
"It's not Anna I'm worried about.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:48.019
What if we let them get close again and the
feelings are too much for Elsa?

00:02:48.019 --> 00:02:50.769
Joy brings her powers out as strongly as fear."

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:54.773
"But if anyone can find a way to help her,
it's Anna."

00:02:54.773 --> 00:02:56.080
"You may be right about that.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.080
There's not much that girl can't do."

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:04.620
"Oh, her love could hold up the world.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.350
OK, we'll tell her when we return."

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.340
"Oh!

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:14.470
Thank you so much for that."

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.349
"They believed in you Anna.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:18.349
And so do I."

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:23.129
This scene was meant to address the idea that
Anna has always felt insecure about her parents'

00:03:23.129 --> 00:03:25.860
decision not to tell her about Elsa's powers.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:29.830
And it could have been a beautiful moment
that boosted her belief in herself, setting

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:32.930
her up even better to become Queen of Arendelle.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:38.340
On top of that, when Elsa tells Anna:
"They believed in you Anna, and so do I",

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.819
the cut scene would have mirrored perfectly
what Anna said to Elsa earlier in the film:

00:03:42.819 --> 00:03:44.569
"I believe in you, Elsa.

00:03:44.569 --> 00:03:46.230
More than anyone or anything."

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:50.390
The deleted scene may have also gone some
way to address some people's criticisms from

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:55.190
the first movie about Agnarr and Iduna's parenting
skills and their decision to keep the sisters

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.540
separated from each other.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:01.860
Another big change to the film's finale was
that, originally, it wasn't going to include

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.739
Kristoff proposing to Anna.

00:04:03.739 --> 00:04:09.040
Indeed, Kristoff almost had a radically different
character arc in Frozen 2, which started with

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.630
his proposal to Anna happening early in the
movie rather than at the very end.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:18.140
In earlier versions of the movie, Kristoff
had an elaborate grand proposal and song planned

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:23.430
for Anna in the castle gardens which then
turned into a charming duet for the couple.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.910
"So you're a lord now."

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.230
"Uh, yeah."

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.900
"And here we are."

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:29.930
"Is it hot out here?"

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.620
"I don't know, erm..
but I think it's romantic."

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.620
"Is it?"

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.620
"Well I thought..
kind of"

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:37.500
"I mean, yeah, er..
and here we are..

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.190
I'm feeling very er..
romantic..

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:40.630
cos it is romantic.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.229
And I guess I..

00:04:42.229 --> 00:04:44.630
I, I wanted to ask you..

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.840
"Ah huh."
"..something."

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:46.840
"Yes!

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:47.840
I mean er..

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:48.840
OK."

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:49.840
"Why is this so hard?"

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:51.050
"This is hard?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.050
I'm sorry..

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.050
I..

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:54.050
I didn't mean.."

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.050
"No, no, no!"

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.050
It's not you, it's me."

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:57.050
"Ahhh.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.120
Hey, what do you think the odds are he turns
out to be a deranged murderer,

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:03.990
and tries to kill you like the last guy she
tried to marry?"

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:09.210
There are lots of intriguing moments and details
in this deleted scene and song, such as the

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:13.210
fact that Kristoff is now a lord;
how it's Anna who ends up actually popping

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:16.419
the question;
and Olaf's savage joke to Elsa about whether

00:05:16.419 --> 00:05:18.810
Kristoff will turn out like Prince Hans.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:23.590
The scene is obviously a lot of fun and full
of much more spectacle than Kristoff's sweet

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:29.660
and simple proposal in the final film:
"Anna, you are the most extraordinary person

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:30.850
I've ever known.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:34.460
I love you with all I am.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:36.600
Will you marry me?"

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.010
"Oh.

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.430
Yes!"

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:43.180
But ultimately, the filmmakers have said that
they decided to take the idea of Kristoff

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:47.860
struggling with proposing to Anna and extend
it over the whole film instead.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.850
Kristoff's original arc through the rest of
the movie had him keeping secrets from Anna

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:55.669
about how he was unhappy with his new position
in Arendellian high society.

00:05:55.669 --> 00:06:00.350
And I'll go into more details about that in
my other Frozen 2 deleted scenes video.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:06.020
Now, if Arendelle Castle was destroyed in
the original ending for Frozen 2, it indicates

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:10.751
that Elsa wasn't resurrected in time to save
the kingdom or, as some rumours for early

00:06:10.751 --> 00:06:15.000
test screenings suggest, there's a version
of the ending in which Elsa never came back

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.130
to life.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:20.970
In the actual movie, after Elsa unfreezes
she falls into the depths of the icy water

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:25.699
beneath Ahtohallan and, if you look closely,
you can see the Nokk looking on.

00:06:25.699 --> 00:06:29.900
Concept art from The Art of Frozen 2 book
shows the water spirit lifting the unconscious

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:34.650
Elsa from the water in a deleted scene that
might imply that Elsa didn't make it.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:38.530
And there's a moment from the secret room
deleted scene I mentioned earlier that could

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:41.930
support the theory that Disney were considering
killing off Elsa.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:48.400
"I can find no record of a human with power
like hers but for the ancient myths with their

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.190
tragic fates."

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:53.890
There's also something strange about the final
epilogue scene in Arendelle.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:58.479
In the scene, Anna unveils a statue in tribute
to her mother and father, but Elsa isn't there

00:06:58.479 --> 00:06:59.729
to share the moment.

00:06:59.729 --> 00:07:04.200
And the earlier part of the scene feels like
it was originally going to be Anna's coronation

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:08.819
day given the very formal green gown, cape,
and crown she's wearing.

00:07:08.819 --> 00:07:16.400
"Presenting Her Majesty, Queen Anna of Arendelle!"

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.620
And just how dressed up Kristoff, Olaf and
Sven are.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:24.270
Again, if this was originally Anna's coronation
day, then it seems a little out of character

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:28.250
for Elsa to miss her sister's special moment,
given how close they are.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:32.520
And even if the scene was always meant to
just be a statue unveiling for their parents,

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:35.750
it still feels slightly amiss for Elsa not
to be there.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:40.040
Still, ultimately, it seems like Elsa remaining
dead at the end of the movie would have been

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:44.030
an unlikely decision for Disney given just
how popular she is.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:49.050
At most, they might have contemplated reviving
her in a post-credits scene or perhaps teasing

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:54.569
her resurrection in a third movie via an end-credits
sting or some other hint, but even that feels

00:07:54.569 --> 00:07:59.729
too much for an animated Disney film, given
a third movie could be up to 6 years away.

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:05.440
More probable is that, in the original ending,
Elsa wasn't going to recover quite so quickly.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:09.830
So, after the Nokk pulled an unconscious Elsa
from the water we would have been led to assume

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:10.889
she was dead.

00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:15.030
This would have been followed by Arendelle
being hit by the wave destroying the castle;

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:18.910
then, in the aftermath, Elsa would finally
have come back to life.

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:23.050
This ending would have been more impactful
and darker given the destruction in Arendelle

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:26.919
and Elsa remaining dead for longer than she
did in the final movie.

00:08:26.919 --> 00:08:31.740
We've also got many other deleted scenes in
Frozen 2 that would have changed other parts

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:32.740
of the story massively.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:38.270
I'll be going into more detail about the castle's
secret room, Olaf's amazing deleted song,

